Cache stable_type_symbol_hash() for concrete types.

stable_type_symbol_key() serialises the entire type graph reachable from a type
into one string and hashes it, and scope_gc_pin_pregen() asks for that hash for
every pinned variable of every call statement, for every `-prod` build that
targets a Boehm GC mode. Nothing memoises it, so a bootstrap compiler built with
`-gc none` (V's own default) leaks megabytes per statement while compiling
`cmd/v` with `-prod -gc boehm`, or any large program with the default GC mode.
On 32-bit that exhausts the address space (https://github.com/vlang/v/issues/28612).
The hash of a concrete type cannot depend on the generic context, so it is cached
once per compilation, shared between the per-file cgen instances. Generated C is
unchanged.

--- vlib/v/gen/c/utils.v.original
+++ vlib/v/gen/c/utils.v
@@ -12,9 +12,41 @@
 const cgen_scope_var_type_cache_salt = u64(0xc2b2ae3d27d4eb4f)
 
 // stable_type_symbol_hash returns a deterministic hash for generated helper names.
+//
+// stable_type_symbol_key walks every type reachable from `typ` and serialises the whole
+// graph into one string, which is then hashed. scope_gc_pin_pregen asks for the hash of
+// the same few types for every call statement it visits, so for a variable of a large
+// struct type (an AST node, say) that is megabytes of temporary strings per statement.
+// A compiler built with `-gc none` (what V's own bootstrap stages use) never frees them,
+// which is enough to exhaust a 32-bit address space while compiling `cmd/v` itself with
+// `-prod -gc boehm`. So cache the hash of concrete types: their descriptor cannot depend
+// on the current generic context (unwrap_generic and recheck_concrete_type leave them,
+// and everything they reach, untouched), hence the cache needs no clearing from
+// clear_type_resolution_caches, and it is shared between the per-file Gens of a
+// parallel cgen so that each descriptor is built once per compilation.
 fn (mut g Gen) stable_type_symbol_hash(typ ast.Type) u64 {
+	cacheable := typ != 0 && !typ.has_flag(.generic) && !g.type_has_unresolved_generic_parts(typ)
+	if cacheable {
+		mut cached := u64(0)
+		mut found := false
+		rlock g.stable_type_symbol_hash_cache {
+			if h := g.stable_type_symbol_hash_cache[typ] {
+				cached = h
+				found = true
+			}
+		}
+		if found {
+			return cached
+		}
+	}
 	mut seen := map[string]bool{}
-	return fnv1a.sum64_string(g.stable_type_symbol_key(typ, mut seen))
+	hash := fnv1a.sum64_string(g.stable_type_symbol_key(typ, mut seen))
+	if cacheable {
+		lock g.stable_type_symbol_hash_cache {
+			g.stable_type_symbol_hash_cache[typ] = hash
+		}
+	}
+	return hash
 }
 
 // stable_type_symbol_key builds a stable type descriptor without using table registration ids.
